{# THE PERIOD, AS A SEGMENTED GROUP.

   RULED: a reader who wants this quarter should not have to open a menu to
   get it. The three that matter are buttons; everything earlier is behind
   the chip beside them. The period a page currently means is named in its
   subline and nowhere else — a group that also printed it would say the
   same thing twice and disagree the first time one of them was wrong.

   LINKS, NOT BUTTONS IN A FORM. Each segment is an address, so the period
   is in the URL and a browser can go back to it, and the whole control
   works with no script of ours.

   Variables:
     kinds   value => label for the three segments
     chosen  which of them is on
     urls    value => the address that segment goes to, one entry per value
             above and per entry in `earlier`
     earlier value => label for the chip's menu, in the order they read #}
<label class="ov-ctl sm pd">
    <span class="k">Period</span>
    <span class="pdrow">
        <span class="periodpick" role="group" aria-label="Period">
            {% for value, label in kinds %}
                <a class="{{ value == chosen ? 'on' : '' }}" href="{{ urls[value] }}"
                   {{ value == chosen ? 'aria-current="true"' : '' }}>{{ label }}</a>
            {% endfor %}
        </span>

        {% if earlier|default([]) is not empty %}
            {# AN EARLIER PERIOD IS A PLACE, so the chip is the house's own
               grouped dropdown: every option a link, no script of ours. #}
            <details class="i-dd">
                <summary class="mchip i-ddt{{ custom|default(false) ? ' on' : '' }}">
                    <span class="i-ddval">{{ custom|default(false) ? customLabel : 'custom&hellip;'|raw }}</span>
                    <span class="i-ddcaret">&#9662;</span>
                </summary>
                <div class="i-ddmenu">
                    <span class="i-ddhead">an earlier period</span>
                    {% for value, label in earlier %}
                        <a class="i-ddopt{{ value == chosen ? ' on' : '' }}" href="{{ urls[value] }}">
                            <span class="i-ddopt-l">{{ label }}</span>
                        </a>
                    {% endfor %}
                </div>
            </details>
        {% endif %}
    </span>
</label>
